        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d36ca98b-f1f0-58b1-9b2d-20ca8292c583",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Klitgaarden, Skagen, Jutland\n- People: Ulrik Plesner, King Christian X, Queen Alexandrine, Alexandrine of Mecklenburg-Schwerin\n- Roles: Danish royal family, Queen of Denmark, Queen of Iceland\n\nFacts:\n- Queen Alexandrine, also known as Alexandrine of Mecklenburg-Schwerin, was born on 24 December 1879 and died on 28 December 1952.\n- Klitgaarden is a former summer residence of the Danish royal family located just south of Skagen on the northern tip of Jutland.\n- Ulrik Plesner designed Klitgaarden for King Christian X and Queen Alexandrine.\n- Klitgaarden was completed in 1914.\n- Queen Alexandrine was Queen of Denmark as the spouse of King Christian X.\n- Queen Alexandrine also held the title of Queen of Iceland.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "5c3b1145-1878-5515-a5f7-132e97210835",
        "text": "Klitgaarden (lit.\"The Dune House\") is a former summer residence of the Danish royal family situated just south of Skagen on the northern tip of Jutland, the house was designed by Ulrik Plesner, and completed in 1914, for King Christian X and Queen Alexandrine, Alexandrine of Mecklenburg-Schwerin (24 December 1879 – 28 December 1952) was Queen of Denmark as the spouse of King Christian X, she also held the title of Queen of Iceland.",
